{
  "comment": "Task entries for tools/stack_budget.py. stack_bytes is a number or an sdkconfig key. A numeric stack cites its source as [file, regex]; tests/test_stack_budget.py checks that the regex's group matches it. envs lists the release envs that link the task; omit it for every env.",
  "overhead_bytes": {
    "comment": "Carved from every task stack by the pinned ESP-IDF Xtensa port: the interrupt frame XT_STK_FRMSZ (192 on both chips) plus the coprocessor save area XT_CP_SIZE rounded up to 16 (96 on ESP32, 316 to 320 on ESP32-S3). Values from xtensa_context.h and port.c uxInitialiseStackCPSA. No TLS section and no task wrapper in release builds.",
    "esp32": 288,
    "esp32s3": 512
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "name": "main",
      "entry": "^void app_main\\(\\)$",
      "stack_bytes": "CONFIG_ESP_MAIN_TASK_STACK_SIZE"
    },
